    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34496" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπορπ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fasten with a brooch</i> or <i>pin</i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵματα ἐνεπορπέατο</span> (
				Ion.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ηντο</span>) they
			<i>wore</i> garments <i>fastened with a brooch upon the
			shoulder</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.77
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπεπορπημένος διπλᾶ τὰ ἱμάτια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lycurg.
					40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				17
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπεπορπημένοι ὠμότητα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>3 Ma.</u>
					7.5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
